            <ArticleTitle>[Medical progress exemplified by improvements in the safety coronary angioplasty].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1361-7; discussion 1367-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The significant decrease in complications associated with coronary angioplasty is a model of medical progress. Breakthroughs are achieved through individual initiatives, whereas incremental progress results from occasional, anonymous improvements. The two types of improvement are complementary, as pointed out by Claude Bernard as early as 1864.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
